{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0092","billNumberShort":"H.B. 92","billNumberLong":"HB0092","fileNumber":"2026FL0236","shortTitle":"Presidential Electors Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"STODDA","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Stoddard, Andrew","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill modifies provisions governing the distribution of electoral votes.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>in an election for president and vice president of the United States:<hr><ltbullet1>allocates one electoral vote for the presidential and vice presidential candidates who receive the highest number of votes in a Congressional district;<hr><ltbullet1>allocates two electoral votes for the presidential and vice presidential candidates who receive the highest number of statewide votes; and<hr><ltbullet1>requires a registered political party, or an unaffiliated candidate or a write-in candidate for president of the United States, to notify the lieutenant governor if a vacancy occurs in the office of a presidential elector; <hr><ltbullet>standardizes the deadlines to file a declaration of candidacy for the office of vice president of the United States and to choose presidential electors; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Michael Cipriano","fiscalAnalyst":"Ivan D. Djambov","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"DJVVAAIANV","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-29 10:53:31.800","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Resear